# What is the difference between a "function" and a "method"?

I am new to programming and I am confused about the difference between a function and a method. From what I've gathered, they are the same thing, but can someone please explain the difference to me? I would appreciate any help.

• ## 7 Answers

A function is a block of code that performs a specific task. A method is a function that is a member of an object. For example, the following is a function:

function add(x, y)
{
return x + y;
}


The following is a method:

function add(x, y)
{
return x + y;
}

var obj = {};
obj.add = add;


